  "source_target_review": "Manual source-target review for second-batch download owner. Unchanged service entry, wrappers, mailbox helpers and bus constructors retain the first-batch proof: services_main reaches one static firmware_owner, initialized only by a138_ble_business_firmware_init using a138_business_mmio_bus and a138_record_mmio_bus. Each constructor binds its own two static MMIO adapters, copied once by a138_ble_business_init; no reachable source reassigns those fields or supplies another bus. Changed owner C/header add one fixed transfer structure, bounded range/ACK/combined/replay/timeout policy and INSPECT. The added a138_record_data_request_facts reads only owner.data, checks the original complete mailbox key before dispatch, and cannot install callbacks. Existing submit stages one additional flags word; result reads add fixed CRC/admission facts. All bus-typed callers conservatively include both static read/write targets for their corresponding type. The only newly reachable indirect caller is a138_record_data_request_facts, explicitly assigned the same record_mmio_read/write closure. There is no PCM copying loop, heap, recursive callback, owner reentry or enabled interrupt. New read policy commits combined ACK only after an actual hardware read-admitted fact; CRC-valid facts bind pending blocks. Every selected C/header/linker/startup/provenance input, the complete actual RV32 disassembly, and every reachable 32-bit JALR site/target set are hash-bound. Unknown callers, changed inputs or missing machine sites still fail closed. This review is specific to these bytes and does not authorize future changes. Reviewed runtime source extensions: ui_runtime.c adds memcmp exclusively under A138_CLASSIC_RUNTIME; ui_main.c factors the existing business init/pump calls through static background wrappers and selects Classic only under that macro. A138_CLASSIC_RUNTIME is absent from this legacy business build. The complete actual non-runtime RV32 disassembly still has the identical locked SHA256 4b75454ea9517d560d1c0efef744d5d974965e5060bcffe77ae60318620d8f1c. Only these two source input identities change; every machine callsite and target set is retained.",
